{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And YHWH was wrathful.</b> He became filled with wrath." "<b>For your sake.</b> You caused it for me. And so it says (Psalms 106): ״וַיַּקְצִיפוּ עַל מֵי מְרִיבָה וַיֵּרַע לְמֹשֶׁה בַּעֲבוּרָם״." "<b>It is enough for you.</b> That they should not say: How harsh is the master, and how obstinate and importunate is the student (Sotah 13). Another interpretation — <b>It is enough for you</b>: much is stored away for you from this; great is the goodness hidden away for you (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:51.462648902Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}